# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-autocad-cad-selection-ignores-com-progid — explicit AutoCAD selection must select the versioned COM server
#+STATUS: DONE (alfe 2.2.79, 2026-09-22) -- pending Windows-runner validation
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-autocad-cad-selection-progid

* Context

Reported 2026-09-17 while investigating SCHMS
[[https://fabrik.sncf.fr/gitlab/dmoe-pop/epure/es/schms/-/jobs/507862][job 507862: test-cad-activex:autocad:windows]].
The job invokes =make test-cad-activex-alfe CAD=autocad=, which selects
=--autocad --mode automation=. It fails before loading the tests:

#+begin_example
AutoCAD process exited before READY (exit 4): ATTACHED=0
CREATED=0 [PROCESS-EXITED-BEFORE-READY]
#+end_example

The exiting child is the =cscript.exe= COM bridge, not necessarily
=acad.exe=. This failure does not involve accoreconsole or execution of
AutoLISP ActiveX tests.

* Reproduction and evidence

Under the Windows runner account, in the same RDP session, the standalone
=dev/scripts/cad/test-autocad-com.vbs= diagnostic in the sibling SCHMS
repository tests registration, GetObject and CreateObject.

#+begin_src powershell
cscript.exe //nologo ../schms/dev/scripts/cad/test-autocad-com.vbs AutoCAD.Application.24.1
cscript.exe //nologo ../schms/dev/scripts/cad/test-autocad-com.vbs
#+end_src

The versioned ProgID succeeds:

#+begin_example
PROGID=AutoCAD.Application.24.1
CLSID={AA46BA8A-9825-40FD-8493-0BA3C4D5CEB5}
ATTACHED=0
CREATEOBJECT.START=17/09/2026 18:02:41
CREATEOBJECT.END=17/09/2026 18:03:22
CREATED=1
AUTOCAD.VERSION=24.1s (LMS Tech)
RESULT=SUCCESS
#+end_example

Its LocalServer32 points to AutoCAD 2022's =acad.exe /Automation=.
The 41-second activation is a successful cold start, not the CI failure.
An initial GetObject error is expected when no accessible instance exists.

The generic ProgID fails immediately:

#+begin_example
PROGID=AutoCAD.Application
CLSID={0DECFB78-73C3-47C7-9630-A1B55B3ACA1C}
LOCALSERVER32.ERROR.HEX=0x80070002
ATTACHED=0
GETOBJECT.ERROR.DECIMAL=429
GETOBJECT.ERROR.DESCRIPTION=ActiveX component can't create object
CREATEOBJECT.START=17/09/2026 18:05:08
CREATEOBJECT.END=17/09/2026 18:05:08
CREATED=0
CREATEOBJECT.ERROR.DECIMAL=429
CREATEOBJECT.ERROR.DESCRIPTION=ActiveX component can't create object
#+end_example

The generic registration resolves to a different CLSID with no readable
LocalServer32 entry; selecting the working versioned registration avoids it.
The successful RDP probe does not independently establish that the CI job
uses the same Windows session, but the generic creation failure reproduces
its bootstrap symptoms under the runner account.

* Problem and cause

=apply-cad-selection= in =autolisp-front-end/source/cli.lisp= resolves
=--cad autocad-2022= to the installed =acad-2022= executable, exports
=AUTOCAD_EXE= and defaults to automation mode. It does not select a COM ProgID.

The VBScript templates in
=autolisp-front-end/source/backend-autocad.lisp= hardcode
=AutoCAD.Application= in GetObject/CreateObject, including the quit bridge.
Automation starts =cscript.exe=; COM registration determines the application
server. Thus choosing an executable does not actually constrain the COM
server to the requested AutoCAD release. With several installations it may
also attach to or create a different release.

* Proposal

Carry the resolved AutoCAD selection through to the automation backend and
resolve its versioned COM ProgID. For AutoCAD 2022, use
=AutoCAD.Application.24.1= consistently for attach, create and cleanup.
Resolve against installed registration/version metadata rather than assuming
all product years follow one arithmetic version mapping.

An explicit release selection must not silently fall back to the generic
ProgID or attach to another release. If no matching COM registration exists,
report the requested release, ProgID and reason clearly. Define and document
the behavior of unversioned =--autocad= and any explicit ProgID override.

Preserve the bridge's COM error number (decimal and hexadecimal) and
Err.Description in the bootstrap error even when activation exits before
READY. Name the failed bridge/activation stage accurately; do not describe
cscript's exit as proof that acad.exe exited.

* Acceptance criteria

- =alfe --cad autocad-2022 --mode automation= selects
  =AutoCAD.Application.24.1= for GetObject and CreateObject, even when the
  generic =AutoCAD.Application= registration is broken or targets another
  release.
- Cleanup uses the same resolved ProgID and retains existing ownership rules
  for attached versus created instances.
- An explicit release never silently selects another AutoCAD COM server.
  Missing/mismatched registration fails with an actionable diagnostic.
- Batch selection remains unchanged: =--cad autocad-2022 --mode batch= uses
  =accoreconsole-2022= and does not depend on COM registration.
- Add failing regression coverage before implementation for CLI selection,
  emitted attach/create/quit bridges, unavailable registration and preservation
  of the original COM failure details. Pure tests run without installed CAD
  on both SBCL and CCL.
- Validate on the Windows runner with broken generic registration and valid
  AutoCAD 2022 registration; record the actual application version and
  executable and run the SCHMS ActiveX tests beyond bootstrap.
- Document selection/fallback/override behavior in alfe's user manual, help,
  man page and specifications as applicable before closing the issue.

* Resolution -- alfe 2.2.79

** The COM server follows the selected release

=resolve-autocad-progid= (=source/backend-autocad.lisp=) answers what
the bridges ask COM for:

1. =$AUTOCAD_PROGID=, verbatim and unchecked -- the escape hatch for a
   release alfe has never heard of;
2. the release's own ProgID -- from =--cad autocad-YYYY=, or failing
   that from the release named in the discovered executable's path --
   confirmed against the registration: a CLSID whose =LocalServer32= is
   readable. That is exactly what the evidence above distinguishes: the
   generic ProgID HAS a CLSID and no readable LocalServer32;
3. the generic =AutoCAD.Application=.

=*autocad-release-com-versions*= maps 2019-2026 to 23.0-25.1. It is a
TABLE, not a formula (2020 is 23.1, 2021 is 24.0, 2025 is 25.0), and it
only proposes: the registry decides, and a release outside the table is
resolved from the registered ProgIDs whose =LocalServer32= names it.

Step 3 is unreachable when the user named the release: that is
=BACKEND-NOT-AVAILABLE=, code =:AUTOCAD-PROGID-UNAVAILABLE=, listing
each ProgID tried with its reason (=not-registered=, =no-local-server=,
=version-not-confirmed=) and pointing at =$AUTOCAD_PROGID=. Explicitness
is read from =cli-options-cad=, so =--autocad= alone still falls back
rather than failing.

The registry is read through =*registry-value-function*= and
=*registry-progids-function*= (reg.exe on Windows), which is what lets
the tests describe registrations on any host.

** Both bridges, one server

=emit-bridge-vbs= and =emit-quit-vbs= take =:progid=; the templates
carry the ProgID placeholder where the generic ProgID was hardcoded.
The session keeps the resolved ProgID, so SHUTDOWN quits the instance
this run created and not another release's.

** The COM failure is no longer thrown away

The bridge writes =COM.PROGID=, =COM.STAGE= (=getobject= /
=createobject=), =COM.ERROR.DECIMAL=, =COM.ERROR.HEX= and
=COM.ERROR.DESCRIPTION= to its error file, capturing =Err.Number= /
=Err.Description= into locals first -- the next statement clears them.
An expected attach miss under =auto= goes to the debug trace, not to
the error file. =%autocad-await-ready= reads that file and
=summarize-process-exit= reports it:

#+begin_example
AutoCAD COM bridge (cscript) exited before READY (exit 4) at createobject(AutoCAD.Application.24.1): COM error 429 (0x1AD) ActiveX component can't create object
  The COM bridge is what exited; whether acad.exe started is what ATTACHED/CREATED say.
  Server asked for: AutoCAD.Application.24.1 (override with $AUTOCAD_PROGID).
#+end_example

The old message -- "AutoCAD process exited before READY (exit 4):
ATTACHED=0 CREATED=0" -- both lost the diagnosis and claimed something
unobserved about acad.exe.

** Tests (alfe suite, SBCL and CCL, no CAD required)

- the requested release resolves to its versioned ProgID, from =--cad=
  and from the executable's own path;
- an explicit release with no usable registration signals, naming the
  release, the ProgID and =$AUTOCAD_PROGID= -- and does NOT return the
  generic one;
- =--autocad= without a release never fails: versioned when registered,
  generic otherwise;
- =$AUTOCAD_PROGID= is used verbatim, registry or no registry;
- both emitted bridges carry the resolved ProgID and no bare generic
  COM call;
- the bridge template records the COM stage/number/hex/description;
- the bootstrap message reports 429 / 0x1AD / the description / the
  ProgID / the stage, says "bridge", and no longer says "AutoCAD
  process exited";
- batch emission reads no registry at all (the readers are bound to
  functions that signal if called).

Seen RED before the fix: with the resolver short-circuited to the
generic ProgID, 4 checks fail across those tests.

** Documentation

alfe user manual: /Which AutoCAD automation actually talks to/ (the
resolution table and the no-fallback rule), =$AUTOCAD_PROGID= among the
environment variables, and two troubleshooting entries. Man page:
=AUTOCAD_PROGID=. alfe specifications: the ProgID resolution order and
the recorded COM failure fields. RELEASE_NOTES.org under /CAD
selection/.

** Still open -- the Windows runner

The acceptance criterion "validate on the Windows runner with broken
generic registration and valid AutoCAD 2022 registration, record the
actual application version and executable, run the SCHMS ActiveX tests
beyond bootstrap" needs the machine and the SCHMS job (507862). Nothing
here was exercised against a real AutoCAD; what is proven is the
selection, the emitted bridges and the diagnostics.
